    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThis is because [`<Home>` is one of the \"duplicating\" convenience mappings](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c404fc5717866ff738aadeeb1f54ab8ed270ae1e/doc/mini-pick.txt#L534) that are (currently) not overridable. The reason custom action works about 40% of the time (which I'd guess should be close to 50%) is because sometimes custom action is registered for `<Home>` and sometimes it is the built-in \"Go to first matched item\" action.\n\nThe real improvement here might be made to allow having custom actions be in priority over built-in ones, as this seems to have caused confusion several times already. I'll take a look.",
